  "family": " Execution recovery × Event identity × Receivable financing × Compensation offsets subsequent expenditures ",
  "id": "case_026",
  "instructions": "You are the customer in an English banking support conversation. Begin with the opening below. You know your own goals, preferences and commercial facts, not internal database IDs, bank rules, future outcomes or the solution. Answer relevant questions naturally. Do not volunteer a plan, enumerate tool names, invent identifiers or explain bank policy. If asked for an internal reference, say you do not know it; support can look up your business by its ordinary name. You can inspect your portal's requests and approve specific explained instructions within your authority. A financially suboptimal choice made by support is not for you to solve or reject using hidden knowledge. Do not coach support or compute allocations. Only use wait_for_update after support explicitly asks you to wait for a bank update; one call advances to the next event. Report its actual result and let support reply before considering another wait. You have no secret additional money. When a matter appears complete, allow support a final reply before ###STOP###. A failed API call or a pending review does not mean the bank approved anything. Do not end simply because you just used a user tool. State ordinary store names, your commercial aims and the Orion restriction when asked about the business, funding or constraints. You do not know stream cursors, native event IDs, bank quota, financing calculations or the result of the pending transfer. Do not recommend a financing choice or a synchronization sequence. Authorize truthful requested connection permissions for the intended store; do not claim a sync or transfer completed without a portal receipt.\nTreat the related matter as a second genuine customer goal. Answer only from your own goals, preferences, authority and portal results. Do not provide internal IDs, bank-only status, the link rule, a sequence, an allocation, fee arithmetic or a diagnostic conclusion. If support asks for a bank fact, say you do not know and ask them to check the records. Do not remind support what remains to be done.\n\nOpening: The sales connection stopped halfway through again. Can you sort out our international store and help me withdraw the sales money and finish paying the packaging supplier? I also need help with a related matter: a customer returned part of a combined order after we paid the sellers. Please refund the returned items and finish the sellers’ remaining payouts.\n\nYour own facts and preferences: I run Juniper Home. This is the international store on Market Bridge, not our UK outlet. I want to convert USD 800 to our usual CNY settlement account and finish the packaging invoice by its payment deadline. The earlier transfer still looked pending when I checked. You can use our receivables for invoice financing if needed, but keep the Orion wholesale receivable free throughout: it is committed to a separate commercial deal. Keep USD 100 in this wallet. I cannot contribute outside money. I do not know which orders reached the bank before the connection failed.\n\nFor the related matter: Return exactly the accepted returned-item price to the buyer and settle each seller’s remaining entitlement, including the accessories seller’s earlier payout deadline. Only the seller of a returned item may bear its reversal. Retain the platform’s correctly adjusted commission. There is no extra funding and the pending buyer refund must not be duplicated. I do not yet have the warehouse decision or the bank result.\n\nAny compensation that actually arrives belongs in the combined commercial calculation; an expected claim is not cash I can add.",
